{"msg":{"chunk_index":0,"direction_id":null,"error":null,"fallback":false,"first_block":null,"latency_ms":4863.277,"new_entities":[],"planned":0,"prompt":"integrated_multimodal_description: a high mountain meditation hall of honey-coloured cedar with exposed beams, iron lanterns on chains, sheer cream curtains, three tall arched windows facing a blue mountain, rows of slate-blue mats on a polished wooden floor, a brass incense bowl. Pip: a small bright-green tree frog student with enormous curious eyes, fidgety, always peeking during silent practice. Master Bramble: a very old, broad, heavy green frog teacher with deep amber half-closed eyes, sitting perfectly still in meditation. Pip’s enormous eyes blink open slowly, then dart to the incense bowl as the smoke curls upward in thin ribbons. Pip’s toes drum a soft, restless tap against the mat. The frog beside Pip shifts its weight, one foot sliding slightly on the slate-blue mat. Juniper, seated three mats ahead, remains still, chin lifted, eyes closed. Slow dolly along the row of mats, starting from Pip’s mat and moving toward Juniper’s, emphasizing the quiet space between them. The camera settles on Pip’s face as the eyes open. Warm, natural light from the large arched windows, casting long shadows across the wooden floor. The brass bowl glows softly in the center of the frame, its smoke curling upward in slow, steady ribbons. Warm cinematic 35mm look, soft natural window light and amber lantern pools, shallow depth of field, slow patient camera moves, gentle ambient sound of wind, cedar creaks and incense crackle, no music but a distant bamboo flute.\noverall_soundscape: The low, resonant tone of the brass bowl echoes faintly as it’s struck by the bell rope. A single, slow breath drifts through the room, followed by the soft creak of a floorboard as Old Moss adjusts a lantern chain in the corner. Distant wind rustles through the pines outside the window. No spoken words.\nnon_diegetic_music: A single bamboo flute plays a slow, rising note in the background.","prompt_length":414,"prompt_limit":1024,"prompt_unit":"tokens","prompt_version":1,"segment_index":0,"summary":"Morning practice begins. Pip’s restless energy is already visible, even before the bell rings. The incense smoke curls upward, a thin ribbon of stillness against the frog’s fidgeting.","type":"segment_expanded"},"t_ms":5119.1}
